# Test: an operator's unrelated commit does not orphan a live ddos local drop
# rule. The cap still removes it after the reload, proven by an nft readback and
# by `show ddos local` while the flood is still running.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-ddos-timing-leaves-reach-no-worker AC-6 across a config apply.
#            A drop rule installed before the reload is still known to the
#            responder the apply builds (register.go replaceResponder ->
#            responder.go adoptMitigation), so the plugin's worker
#            (startMaxDurationWorker -> enforceMaxDuration -> removeMitigation)
#            reaches it and the kernel loses the rule.
# PREVENTS:  the config apply building a fresh idle responder over a live rule.
#            The firewall registry is keyed by table name, so the kernel keeps
#            ze_ddos-local after the responder that installed it is dropped. Both
#            removal paths return on !active -- enforceMaxDuration and onCleared
#            alike -- so the drop would be bounded by neither the cap nor a clear
#            and the box would blackhole the victim for the life of the daemon
#            while `show ddos local` reported no mitigation. One ordinary commit
#            on any ddos local leaf reaches that state.
#
# WHAT THE PROBE WATCHES FOR. Two outcomes, in one poll. The ORPHAN is the kernel
# holding the rule while `show ddos local` reports no mitigation: that state is
# reachable only after the apply, and it is terminal. The PASS is the cap
# removing the rule after the reload, read back from the kernel and from the
# daemon. `ddos-local: reconfigured` below is the third half: it is what says the
# apply ran at all, so a reload that never landed cannot be read as a pass.
#
# WHAT THE RELOAD CHANGES. `confidence-min`, which gates a CHARACTERIZED
# mitigation. characterize-enable is false, so the leaf reaches the plugin and
# touches no drop rule: the reload is exactly the unrelated commit this test is
# about.
#
# WHY THE FLOOD NEVER STOPS. The removal is asserted while the probe is still
# flooding, so no AttackCleared can have arrived: the detector needs
# clear-consecutive-checks evaluations under the threshold, which the config puts
# at 100. The cap is the only path left, which is what makes the assertion
# discriminate.
#
# WHY THE CAP IS 20. The rule must still be live when the reload lands, and the
# reload is one file write and one signal after the install is observed. Twenty
# seconds leaves the apply room to complete while the rule is up, and still ends
# the test inside its own timeout.
#
# STATUS: a Linux/QEMU integration test; NOT executable on the darwin dev host.
#   It needs a fully privileged host and two capability families.
#     - net-admin: ddos-local writes the nftables table, and the probe reads it
#       back through netlink.
#     - bpf (CAP_BPF + CAP_SYS_RESOURCE): the traffic-usage block drives
#       rlimit.RemoveMemlock() and link.AttachTCX()
#       (internal/plugins/trafficusage/attach_linux.go). Without it the victim
#       prefix never resolves, and applyMitigation refuses to install an
#       unscoped rule -- so the test could only fail.
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,bpf
# Serialize against every other ddos test: they all flood the SAME loopback
# interface and the detector picks the victim by top-destination-bytes over that
# interface, so a sibling's concurrent flood is indistinguishable from this
# test's own. Rationale in full: test/plugin/ddos-direction.ci.
option=exclusive:group=ddos-flood
option=env:var=ze.log.ddos.detect:value=info
option=env:var=ze.log.ddos.local:value=info
# 50s to install the drop under a flood, then 40s for the reload and the
# one-second cap worker to reach it, plus daemon startup.
option=timeout:value=180s

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
ddos {
	detect {
		enabled true
		absolute-floor 1000
		confirm-duration 1
		clear-consecutive-checks 100
		startup-grace 0
		baseline-window 10
		check-interval 1
		characterize-enable false
	}
	observe {
		incident-ring-size 100
	}
	local {
		response-level enforce
		max-mitigation-duration 20
	}
}

traffic {
	usage {
		enabled true
		track-ip true
		interfaces {
			interface lo {
				enabled true
			}
		}
	}
}

plugin {
	external ddos-local-cap-survives-reload-probe {
		run "ze-test fixture plugin/ddos-local-cap-survives-reload-driver"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=175s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=RELOAD-CAP-INSTALLED 127.0.0.10
expect=stderr:contains=RELOAD-CAP-REMOVED 127.0.0.10
expect=stderr:contains=ddos-local: drop rule installed
expect=stderr:contains=ddos-local: reconfigured
expect=stderr:contains=ddos-local: max-mitigation-duration reached
